  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": 0,
      "title": "Install Cytoscape 3.10.2",
      "instruction": "Download and install Cytoscape version 3.10.2 on your system; this will be used later to visualize the host‑microbe interaction networks.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 1,
      "title": "Set up computational environment",
      "instruction": "Download the MicrobioLink pipeline from its GitHub repository, then install all required software tools and Python packages (e.g., gget, mygene) so that the command‑line scripts can be executed.",
      "substeps": [
        {
          "instruction": "Clone or download the MicrobioLink repository.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Create and activate a Python virtual environment (optional but recommended).",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Install required packages, for example: `pip install gget mygene` (and any other dependencies listed in the pipeline’s requirements file).",
          "title": ""
        }
      ],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 2,
      "title": "Run functional enrichment analysis",
      "instruction": "Execute the enrichment script with the exact arguments shown below to perform enrichment on the TieDIE‑derived gene list using the Reactome 2022 database.",
      "substeps": [
        {
          "instruction": "Open a terminal and change to the workflow directory:",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "```bash\ncd MicrobioLink2/workflow\n```",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Run the script:",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "```bash\npython enrichr_id_database_ranking.py \\",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "--background_gene_list \"case_study_input/input/human_transcriptomics/enterocyte_colon_CD_expressed_genes.csv\" \\",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "--sep \";\" \\",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "--id_background \"genesymbol\" \\",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "--target_gene_list \"case_study_output/output/TieDIE/tiedie.cn.sif.txt\" \\",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "--analysis_level \"TieDIE\" \\",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "--output_image \"case_study_output/output/Enrichment_analysis/gget_enrichr_results_reactome_usecase_tiedie.png\" \\",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "--output_file \"case_study_output/output/Enrichment_analysis/gget_enrichr_results_reactome_usecase_tiedie.csv\" \\",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "--database \"Reactome_2022\" \\",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "--ranking \"combined_score\"\n```",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "Notes:",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "- The `--background_gene_list` file must contain the full set of expressed genes (first column) using gene symbols (as specified by `--id_background`).",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "- The `--sep` argument defines the delimiter used in the background file; here it is a semicolon (`;`).",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "- Choose `--analysis_level \"TieDIE\"` to enrich downstream signaling genes; alternatively, `\"HMI\"` can be used to enrich directly on human proteins targeted by microbes.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "- The output image will be saved as a PNG (or other graphic format) at the path given by `--output_image`; the table of results will be saved at `--output_file`.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "- The default ranking metric is `combined_score` (natural log of p‑value × z‑score); you may switch to `adj_p` by setting `--ranking \"adj_p\"`.",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "- If you encounter the error `AttributeError: partially initialized module 'charset_normalizer' has no attribute 'md__mypyc'`, verify that the `mygene` package is correctly installed (see troubleshooting 6).",
          "title": ""
        },
        {
          "instruction": "- An empty output file usually indicates mismatched identifiers across input files (e.g., missing UniProt IDs); ensure all files use the same identifier type (see troubleshooting 7).",
          "title": ""
        }
      ],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 3,
      "title": "Inspect enrichment results",
      "instruction": "Open the generated PNG image and CSV file to review the top 20 enriched pathways (combined‑score ranking) and interpret their relevance to the host‑microbe interaction study.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    }
  ],
